at failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 56     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a soft  pink tan piece of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  It is inked and sectioned  to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular tan gritty firm mass abutting the resection margin  A representative sample of the mass is frozen and now submitted in A  The rest of the mass is submitted in B through D  Uninvolved tissues in E  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  INVOLVING THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
