y  sampled  The mass consists of residual osteoid and matrix  without viable  tumor cells seen  There is extensive DCIS in this area  as well as in adjacent  breast tissue   The findings would be classified as a complete pathologic response  a  Miller Payne score of 5  of 5  or a Residual Cancer Burden index of 0  RCB  Class pCR    This carcinoma would also be classified as AJCC  6th edition   yp Tis yp  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   sn    CLINICAL DATA   History  Metaplastic carcinoma of L breast  status post preop chemotherapy   Operation  Left simple mastectomy  sentinel lymph node biopsy   Operative Findings  Not given   Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast cancer   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left sentinel node Biopsy FS   B 2  Left simple mastectomy   stitch on axillary tail   O R  CONSULTATION   Arrival time  1 15 PM  Report time  1 25 PM  SPECIMEN LABELED  1  LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   FSA    One lymph node negative for tumor   OR Consultation by  Lucian Chirieac  M D   Resident  MATTHIAS D  HOFER  MD  The senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a gross and or  microscopic examination of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed  the rapid diagnos es  related thereto   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s  name and unit number   Part A    1  Left sentinel lymph node  Bx   FS   consists of one fragment of  fibroadipose tissue  0 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm   with one lymph node candidate  identified  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen  analysis as FSA   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FSA remnant  2 frags  ESS   Part B    2  Left simple mastectomy   stitch on axillary tail   consists of a  212 gram left simple mastectomy  14 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm   with white tan skin  ellipse  14 5 x 6 5cm   including an areola  4 0cm in diameter  and a nipple   1 3cm in diameter   There is a stitch designed as axillary tail  per  surgeon  In the lower outer quadrant