Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 AUG 97 at 14 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FIELD FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   Note  Definite ductal carcinoma in situ  and blood vascular and lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 18 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 AUG 97 at 08 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of yellow tan tissue  which is cut and sectioned to reveal a firm  gritty  tan white mass that is 0 6cm in greatest dimension with an ill defined border  No frozen section was done  The specimen has been submitted in its entirety in A B  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Yes.
