Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 37 CLINICAL DATA  Cyst     REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Revised on 26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 49                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE  Note  The invasive tumor measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension and is present less than 0 1cm from multiple inked resection margins  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be ordered  SKIN  LEFT SHOULDER   EXCISION  EPIDERMAL INCLUSION CYST  Note  Diagnosed by Dr  H R  Byers  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  no microcalcifications seen on the x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm firm  tan stellate area grossly suspicious for carcinoma but too small to freeze  Submitted entirely in A through G  with suspicious area in C and D  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast cyst  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse overlying a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm relatively thin walled cyst that is filled with dark brown thick material  The skin surface shows a less than 0 1cm in diameter ulceration  The specimen is resected and submitted entirely in AA  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   VERY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION PERFORMED  AT REQUEST OF SURGEON  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B  LEFT BREAST CYST   report_end  , No.
