Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 93 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   98   PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SLIDE G   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   2    Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 93 at 18 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fatty breast with a localizing needle  Separate from this is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fat  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a 0 8cm stellate  retracted area that focally extends to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  The remaining breast tissue is fatty  The lesion with the nearest inked margin is submitted in A through C  Representative sections of the remainder are submitted in E through J  No frozen section done  Resident  Michael Pins  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS CIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  SUBMITTED FOR PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No.
