s of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Left breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal foci of calcification and a small 0 3cm cyst  A small lesion is present with a vague stellate appearance  measuring 0 5cm in greatest size  Frozen section of this lesion is requested by Dr  Gadd  Tissue submitted entirely in A through J with frozen section in J  Received fresh in a second container and designated  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of breast tissue  The tissue is inked black  with a superior surface  short stitch  yellow over black and the lateral surface  long stitch  green over black  The medial surface is inked red over black  Sectioned to reveal a white granular poorly defined area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DA